# Security Rules

See AGENTS/07-security.md for full details. These rules are non-negotiable.

## Credentials
- NEVER hardcode usernames, passwords, API keys, or tokens in TypeScript files
- NEVER commit .env files — they are gitignored
- NEVER use Basic auth with hardcoded fallback defaults
- All sensitive config MUST come from environment variables with startup validation

## XSS Prevention
- NEVER use innerHTML or outerHTML with user-provided content
- NEVER use DomSanitizer.bypassSecurityTrust* unless source is server-controlled
- Always use Angular's template binding ({{ }}, [attr]) for user content

## Nuxeo Auth
- NEVER add Authorization headers manually in components — use the interceptor
- NEVER call Nuxeo URLs with fetch() — use NuxeoApiBase (HttpClient)
- NEVER put credentials in URL query string parameters
- NEVER bind <img [src]> directly to Nuxeo URLs — fetch via service, use blob URL

## Blob URLs
- ALWAYS revoke blob URLs in ngOnDestroy
- Track all created URLs in an array and revoke all of them on destroy

## Secure Coding in Development Agent
When generating new code, proactively apply these rules without being asked:
- Any new config value → from process.env with validation
- Any new image display of Nuxeo content → fetch via service + blob URL
- Any new subscription → takeUntilDestroyed()
- Any new blob creation → tracked array + ngOnDestroy cleanup

## PR blocker
Any of the above violations MUST be fixed before the PR can be merged.
